OOM machinery takes over.
For the Linux Security Modules (LSM) mechanism, though, the kernel does provide a helper routine
to check whether a process can allocate the number of pages being requested, taking into consider -
ation the three VM overcommit policies (the vm.overcommit_memory value). Here is the function: mm/
util.c:__vm_enough_memory().
Firstly, the three VM overcommit policies (with values 0, 1, and 2, respectively) are defined as macros
here:
// include/uapi/linux/mman.h
...
# define OVERCOMMIT_GUESS 0 << this is the default > >
# define OVERCOMMIT_ALWAYS 1
# define OVERCOMMIT_NEVER 2
